{"toolCallId":"call_b516addc53534179a881f86155c8628e","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\n  - \"calculate completeness threshold tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument parser, the two output functions and the trailing exit-code block, and record the exact line where the report finishes so the gate can be placed after it (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T002 Build a throwaway fixture packet in `scratch/` with a known placeholder ratio, and record the percentage the unmodified script reports for it (`specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/scratch/fixture`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T003 Declare the threshold global as empty in the globals block, so an unset value means \"no gate\" (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T004 Add the `--min-percent` case arm before the `*` fallback, with the argument-count guard and the integer 0-100 validation that exits `1` on a bad value (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Add the post-output gate: compare the figure the active mode reports against the threshold and exit `3` below it, `0` at or above it (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Document the option in `show_help` and extend the trailing exit-code comment block to cover `0`, `1` and `3` (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T007 Run the boundary matrix against the fixture: below, exactly at and above the threshold, asserting exit `3`, `0` and `0` respectively (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T008 Diff stdout and stderr from flagged against flagless runs for text, `--json`, `--verbose`, `--quality` and `--file`, and confirm every diff is empty (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T009 Run the malformed-value matrix (missing, non-integer, negative, above 100) and confirm exit `1` each time, plus `bash -n` on the script (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\n  - \"calculate completeness threshold tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument parser, the two output functions and the trailing exit-code block, and record the exact line where the report finishes so the gate can be placed after it (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T002 Build a throwaway fixture packet in `scratch/` with a known placeholder ratio, and record the percentage the unmodified script reports for it (`specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/scratch/fixture`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T003 Declare the threshold global as empty in the globals block, so an unset value means \"no gate\" (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T004 Add the `--min-percent` case arm before the `*` fallback, with the argument-count guard and the integer 0-100 validation that exits `1` on a bad value (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Add the post-output gate: compare the figure the active mode reports against the threshold and exit `3` below it, `0` at or above it (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Document the option in `show_help` and extend the trailing exit-code comment block to cover `0`, `1` and `3` (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T010 Emit the `min_percent_met` boolean in the `--json` report when a threshold is set, true at or above it and false below (REQ-007) (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T007 Run the boundary matrix against the fixture: below, exactly at and above the threshold, asserting exit `3`, `0` and `0` respectively (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T008 Diff stdout and stderr from flagged against flagless runs for text, `--json`, `--verbose`, `--quality` and `--file`, and confirm every diff is empty (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T009 Run the malformed-value matrix (missing, non-integer, negative, above 100) and confirm exit `1` each time, plus `bash -n` on the script (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
